patch=1,EE,000F1870,word,E7AB000C
patch=1,EE,000F1874,word,0808FD41
patch=1,EE,000F1878,word,00000000
//    and only now the hook, so the routine is always written first.
patch=1,EE,0023F4FC,word,0803C600

// 8. Pressing and holding a button both take half as long.
//
//    Two classifiers read the pad's ring of eight button samples, and
//    a ring sample is a world tick, so both of their windows last half
//    as long at 60 fps:
//
//      0x00144E50  held for exactly the last [0x0050B708] samples
//      0x00144CE0  just released, and the run was shorter than the ring
//
//    Measured with injected input: the tackle needs EIGHT ticks both
//    stock and patched, and the game clock at that point reads 233 ms
//    against 133 ms.  Same ticks, half the time.  The tap window halves
//    with it.
//
//    There is no counter to retune.  A differential over all 32 MB of
//    EE RAM -- held against a control that pressed nothing -- found no
//    field anywhere that advances one per tick while a button is down.
//    The state IS the ring.  And the constant cannot carry the fix
//    either: 60 fps needs 14 samples and the ring holds 8; writing 8
//    into 0x0050B708 stops the move coming out at any hold length.
//    Slowing the ring is out too -- it has to turn once per presented
//    frame or the front end loses button edges, which is section 6.
//
//    So both are rewritten in place, around one shared count of
//    consecutive held ticks.  Which one keeps it is not a choice:
//    instrumenting every call site of the evaluator frame by frame
//    shows 0x00144E50 runs on every tick a button is down and
//    0x00144CE0 runs ONLY on the tick it comes up.  So the hold
//    classifier counts, hands the finished run over on release, and
//    the tap classifier reads it.
//
//    Both windows are doubled: the hold fires between 2N and 15, the
//    tap on a run of 13 or fewer, so no tick falls between them.  N is
//    read live from 0x0050B708 rather than baked in, because the ELF
//    ships 5 there and the running game holds 7.
//
//    Verified against stock under identical input: tap up to 200 ms
//    and tackle from 233 ms, against stock's 200 and 233.
//
//    The two tables sit at 0x000F1900, clear of the Freecam mod
//    (0x000F0000..0x000F13AC) and of the rootturn routine above
//    (0x000F1800..0x000F1878).  Cleared once at boot and never again:
//    writing them every frame would reset the count every frame.
patch=0,EE,000F1900,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,000F1904,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,000F1908,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,000F190C,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,000F1910,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,000F1914,word,00000000
