patch=1,EE,00144D50,word,00000000

// 9. taptime -- a 30 Hz mirror of the pad ring.
//
//     0x00144D60 WALKS the ring: from cursor-2 and up to five samples
//     back it looks for one in which the button was up. The ring
//     advances one sample per tick, so those five are 167 ms stock
//     and 83 at 60 fps: the "fresh press" window is worth half.
//     Raising the 5 to 10 is impossible: the ring has eight slots.
//
//     The logic is not rewritten. A counter with a threshold is NOT
//     equivalent: stock fires at +100 ms on a long press and at +34 on
//     a short one, and no threshold does both. What decides is the
//     PATTERN of the last samples, not how long the button was held.
//
//     So the walk stays intact, word for word, and the only thing that
//     changes is WHERE IT READS FROM: a mirror of the ring written at
//     30 Hz. The real ring keeps running at 60 Hz, so just_pressed and
//     just_released still deliver every edge ONCE -- which is what
//     breaks if the whole ring is slowed to 30 Hz.
//
//     The mirror lives at 0x005D7E10, 0x5A00 past the pad array. That
//     distance fits the 16-bit offset of an addiu, and since the pad
//     stride (0x50) is a multiple of 16 the arithmetic holds for all
//     eight ports without dividing anything. The address reads zero in
//     every state checked, has no reference anywhere in .text, leaves
//     0x4D0 bytes of margin and lies past the ELF image, in .bss.
//
//     The mirror ADVANCES the cursor and then writes, just like the
//     real ring: both pad accessors (just_released and pressed_now)
//     read hist[cursor] as the NEWEST sample. Writing first and
//     advancing after would make just_released true on the first frame
//     of the press -- the attack would always come out at 367 ms
//     instead of the 401/434/467 that stock takes depending on how
//     long the button is held.
//
//     Verified against stock, sweeping BOTH things a human finger
//     varies -- when the press lands and how long it lasts -- and with
//     the duration swept again against the moment the attack is
//     accepted.
//
//     The mirror, cleared at boot (640 bytes):
patch=0,EE,005D7E10,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,005D7E14,word,00000000
patch=0,EE,005D7E18,word,00000000
