patch=1,EE,0027E78C,word,0C038860

// 26. scenephase -- what was left of the odd animations: on a CLIP
//     CHANGE there were alternating turns (two on a falling cop, ~80
//     degrees, and one on Cowboy, ~8).
//
//     Same family as rootphase (section 21), but putting rootphase in
//     again does NOT fix it: rootphase takes for granted that the
//     shared cursor still marks the START of the current interval, and
//     that is exactly what breaks.
//
//     0x001044A0 advances the animation with
//
//       new_cursor = trunc((t + dt) * 30 + 0.5)   ; the +0.5 is 0x001044FC
//       advance    = new_cursor - old_cursor
//
//     At 30 fps t*30 lands on the integer and the +0.5 does nothing. At
//     60 fps the half frames appear and when a clip starts 0.5 and 1.5
//     round UP: the cursor at [ctx+0x1C] -- and with it the pointers
//     and counts of every channel -- moves one tick into the future.
//     Later, with the accumulated floating-point error, the half frames
//     land just below the edge and rounding gives the previous integer
//     again: that is why the anomaly is BRIEF and not an alternation
//     through the whole scene.
//
//     With the cursor ahead, the bone interpolator (0x00104AC8)
//     extrapolates from the NEXT pair with a negative factor, and
//     rootphase -- which decides the half frame with t*30 - cursor --
//     sees that negative and does not engage.
//
//     The correction is a quarter tick, BOUNDED by two guards:
//
//       if $ra_of_0x001044A0 == 0x00106AA0 and $f22 == 1/60: arg -= 0.25
//
//     0.25 and not a bare floor: the half integers stay in the previous
//     interval and the integers keep tolerance to land just below the
//     ideal value. It is calibrated for the HALVES of a 30 Hz tick,
//     which is why the dt is CHECKED instead of assumed: [scene+0x0C]
//     scales it before the jal (0x00106A9C), so a clip in slow motion
//     does not take this branch.
//
//     The caller guard is backed by the EXECUTABLE, it is not a list of
//     characters or a heap pointer: 0x00106A80 is the update method of
//     vtable 0x00534D58, whose name method returns the string
//     "Anim Task SceneAnim" at 0x005469E0, and its jal at 0x00106A98
//     returns to 0x00106AA0. The routine reads that return address from
//     the sd $ra, 0($sp) that 0x001044A0 does in its prologue.
//     0x001044A0 has 56 callers and the guard lets one in.
//
//     Measured on root orientation x bone 1:
//
//       Cop, 99 transitions       max 79.98 deg, two jumps > 15 -> max 4.75, none
//       Cowboy, 59 transitions    max  8.14 deg                 -> max 1.063
//       Rembrandt, 149            rootphase already present     -> max 4.49, none
//
//     The delay slot (0x001044FC, add.s $f12, $f12, $f20) is NOT
//     touched and so it does NOT appear below: it runs anyway before
//     the jump -- it is the delay slot of a jal -- and it is the +0.5
//     this routine lowers to +0.25.
//
//     The cave is at 0x000E2100, next to rootphase's
//     (0x000E2000..0x000E2088) without overlapping.
//
//     The routine, disassembled (the patch lines below are the same
//     words):
//
//       0x000E2100  27BDFFD0  addiu $sp, $sp, -48
//       0x000E2104  7FA80000  sq    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000E2108  7FA90010  sq    $t1, 16($sp)
