// 33. doorslide -- SLIDING DOORS open and close at DOUBLE speed.
//
//     The symptom: the Writer's Block elevator door travels its rail in
//     half the time. Measured, from the first movement to the settled
//     sample: stock 7.173 s against 3.588 unfixed.
//
//     It is NOT Lua and NOT the ORDER, it is the TRAVEL. The bytecode
//     of level3_balcony says that C2.OpenEleDoor() only calls
//     OpenDoor(Doors.EleBot), and that C2.ButtonPressed schedules it at
//     30000 - 7000 ms: the order still fires with seven seconds left,
//     patched or not. The native path is OpenDoor 0x00379AC8 ->
//     0x00396EA0 -> message 0x22 with argument 2 (CloseDoor 0x00397010
//     sends the same with 3), and the handler 0x003F5608 wakes the
//     leaves and sends them modes 13/14.
//
//     The cause is in the leaf update, 0x003F5A68, which loads the
//     configured step from [parent_state+0x30] and adds or subtracts it
//     AS IS, without multiplying it by time:
//
//       0x003F5AE0  lwc1 $f0,0x30($v0)   0x003F5AE4  add.s $f0,$f1,$f0
//       0x003F5B2C  lwc1 $f0,0x30($v0)   0x003F5B30  sub.s $f0,$f1,$f0
//
//     The same step per update at 60 Hz is twice as much per second. On
//     the elevator the step is 0.014 and the limit 3 units: ~0.84 u/s
//     against ~0.42.
//
//     And they are PER-DOOR parameters, not game constants: another
//     door has TWO leaves, step 0.01 and limit ~2.31. That is why the
//     section multiplies by 0.5 the step THE INSTRUCTION HAS ALREADY
//     LOADED instead of writing a number -- 0.5 is the only constant
//     that is right for all of them.
//
//     The TWO guards, both reads and neither of them a write:
//
//       1. the global timestep (0x005102CC) is exactly 1/60;
//       2. the LIVE display divider (0x00596D70) is 1.
//
//     The second one is needed: a stock 30 fps session can have the
//     timestep at 1/60 in SLOW MOTION -- SetSlowMo writes that same
//     float -- and halving the door there would make it worse, not
//     better. With the divider at 2 the section is inert and the two
//     original instructions run as they are.
//
//     It keeps the limits, the native comparison, the orders, the
//     waking of the leaves, the callbacks, the geometry and the
//     per-entity configuration. The small overshoot before the clamp
//     already exists in stock: the mechanism is kept and the magnitude
//     shrinks with the smaller step. Both directions end at the native
//     end point and in mode 12.
//
//     Measured, first sample with movement to settled sample:
//
//       elevator opening          stock 7.173  unfixed 3.588  fixed 7.161
//       closing by native order         7.107          3.559        7.129
//       another door, TWO leaves        7.741          3.869        7.724
//
//     The start with this section lands on the same clock as without it
//     (182687, substep 10962), so it does not delay the order to
//     compensate. And stock plus this section gives a trace IDENTICAL to
//     stock: the 661 samples of position and state of parent and leaf,
//     counter, substep and clock all match.
//
//     The two routines, in their caves. They are the same except for
//     the replayed arithmetic and the return site; first OPEN:
//
//       0x000E3800  27BDFFD0  addiu $sp, $sp, -48
//       0x000E3804  7FA10000  sq    $at, 0($sp)
//       0x000E3808  7FA80010  sq    $t0, 16($sp)
//       0x000E380C  C4400030  lwc1  $f0, 48($v0)
//       0x000E3810  3C010051  lui   $at, 0x0051
//       0x000E3814  342102CC  ori   $at, $at, 716
//       0x000E3818  8C280000  lw    $t0, 0($at)
//       0x000E381C  3C013C88  lui   $at, 0x3C88
//       0x000E3820  34218889  ori   $at, $at, -30583
//       0x000E3824  1501000C  bne   $t0, $at, 0x000E3858
//       0x000E3828  00000000  nop
//       0x000E382C  3C010059  lui   $at, 0x0059
//       0x000E3830  34216D70  ori   $at, $at, 28016
//       0x000E3834  90280000  lbu   $t0, 0($at)
//       0x000E3838  24010001  addiu $at, $zero, 1
//       0x000E383C  15010006  bne   $t0, $at, 0x000E3858
//       0x000E3840  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3844  E7A20020  swc1  $f2, 32($sp)
//       0x000E3848  3C013F00  lui   $at, 0x3F00
//       0x000E384C  44811000  mtc1  $at, $f2
//       0x000E3850  46020002  mul.s $f0, $f0, $f2
//       0x000E3854  C7A20020  lwc1  $f2, 32($sp)
//       0x000E3858  7BA10000  lq    $at, 0($sp)
//       0x000E385C  7BA80010  lq    $t0, 16($sp)
//       0x000E3860  27BD0030  addiu $sp, $sp, 48
//       0x000E3864  46000800  add.s $f0, $f1, $f0
//       0x000E3868  080FD6BA  j     0x003F5AE8
//       0x000E386C  00000000  nop
//
patch=1,EE,000E3800,word,27BDFFD0
patch=1,EE,000E3804,word,7FA10000
patch=1,EE,000E3808,word,7FA80010
patch=1,EE,000E380C,word,C4400030
