// 34. scenevel -- Cleon and Fox JERK in the opening cutscene.
//
//     The symptom: in the opening cutscene both characters jump
//     sideways and back. Cleon around 2 s into the clip (keys 61/62),
//     Fox around 2.8 s (keys 85/86).
//
//     The cause is NOT the pose, it is the VELOCITY. 0x00104CE0
//     evaluates the scene animation; its channel 0 -- the one it calls
//     from 0x00104DC4 -- uses the reader 0x00104BC8 to decode
//     TRANSLATION VELOCITY, which is then integrated into the human's
//     physical position. Channel 1 carries POSE translation and its
//     joints keep their interpolation.
//
//     The resource's keys carry a velocity impulse and a pose
//     compensation THAT CANCEL EXACTLY AT 30 Hz. At 60 Hz interpolating
//     the VELOCITY mixes the impulses of two intervals while the pose
//     compensation follows another course: for half a step only part
//     of the velocity that would compensate the pose is applied, and
//     afterwards part of the previous impulse is left over. The
//     composition `physical position + root rotation x pose
//     translation` jumps first one way and then the other.
//
//     Neither the pose alone nor the physical position alone is the
//     visual measure, which is why this does not show up in bone
//     buffers. scenephase's cursors are RIGHT and there is no camera
//     cut at those instants: it is not a leftover of any earlier scene
//     section.
//
//     The correction: for the two half steps that make up a stock
//     interval, take the velocity from the WHOLE END of that interval.
//     That way each half step contributes half of stock's displacement
//     and the pose keeps interpolating:
//
//       reader_time = float(trunc(time_in_keys + 0.75))
//
//     The 0.75 margin picks the NEXT integer from a half key and keeps
//     the current integer against the accumulated floating-point error.
//     It is bounded to SceneAnim's normal cadence: it is not a general
//     rounding of arbitrary velocities. It does not change the real
//     time or the context's cursor. The EE's cvt.w.s always truncates
//     towards zero, so it does not depend on the FCR31 rounding mode.
//
//     The FIVE guards, all reads and none of them writes:
//
//       1. $ra == 0x00104DCC, the channel 0 call and nothing else;
//       2. the parent's return address, at ORIGINAL stack +0x40, is
//          0x00106B7C (SceneAnim). 0x00104CE0 stores it there with the
//          `sd $ra, 0x40($sp)` at 0x00104D20;
//       3. the global timestep (0x005102CC) is exactly 1/60;
//       4. the LIVE display divider (0x00596D70) is 1 -- doorslide's
//          guard: SetSlowMo writes the same float, so dt == 1/60 alone
//          is not enough;
//       5. $f20 == 1.0, normal playback speed.
//
//     THE HOOK GOES ON THE READER'S ENTRY AND NOT ON THE CHANNEL, and
//     that is what keeps cutshift intact: on the half step before the
//     cut cutshift returns zero WITHOUT calling the reader; on the cut
//     it calls with ANOTHER return address, which guard 1 excludes, and
//     doubles the velocity; and after the cut it already hands over a
//     whole time, which this section keeps. The rest of its calls
//     arrive by tail call and keep ra == 0x00104DCC. climbphase stays
//     out for the same reason. The reader has TWO direct callers in the
//     whole .text -- 0x00104DC4 and 0x00104EC0 -- and guard 1 lets one
//     through.
//
//     Measured on the composed root pose. The stock column advances
//     1/30 s and the others 1/60, so their maxima are NOT comparable as
//     speeds: what is compared is the error against stock at the same
//     phase.
//
//       Cleon, 1.94-2.16 s   unfixed 0.32333  fixed 0.01370  stock 0.02590
//         error against stock: 0.16208 -> 0.00403
//       Fox,   2.74-2.96 s   unfixed 0.11239  fixed 0.02860  stock 0.05722
//         error against stock: 0.08538 -> 0.01140
//
//     Regressions: 241 samples of stock plus this section give 2,406
//     observations of position, rotation, channels and contexts
//     identical to stock; 121 samples of neutral gameplay give 1,210
//     identical to the patch without it; and the camera cut regression
//     -- the cop, 71 samples -- gives the same three exact steps,
//     0 / 0.49406072 / 0, with and without this section.
//
//     It preserves the 128-bit $t0/$t1, $f13 as scratch, the stack and
//     the return address; $f12 is the argument it changes on purpose.
//     No mutable state. The routine, in its cave:
//
//       0x000E3E00  27BDFFD0  addiu $sp, $sp, -48
//       0x000E3E04  7FA80000  sq    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000E3E08  7FA90010  sq    $t1, 16($sp)
//       0x000E3E0C  E7AD0020  swc1  $f13, 32($sp)
//       0x000E3E10  3C080010  lui   $t0, 0x0010
//       0x000E3E14  35084DCC  ori   $t0, $t0, 19916
//       0x000E3E18  17E8001E  bne   $ra, $t0, 0x000E3E94
//       0x000E3E1C  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3E20  8FA80070  lw    $t0, 112($sp)
//       0x000E3E24  3C090010  lui   $t1, 0x0010
//       0x000E3E28  35296B7C  ori   $t1, $t1, 27516
//       0x000E3E2C  15090019  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E3E94
//       0x000E3E30  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3E34  3C080051  lui   $t0, 0x0051
//       0x000E3E38  350802CC  ori   $t0, $t0, 716
//       0x000E3E3C  8D080000  lw    $t0, 0($t0)
//       0x000E3E40  3C093C88  lui   $t1, 0x3C88
//       0x000E3E44  35298889  ori   $t1, $t1, -30583
//       0x000E3E48  15090012  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E3E94
//       0x000E3E4C  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3E50  3C080059  lui   $t0, 0x0059
//       0x000E3E54  35086D70  ori   $t0, $t0, 28016
//       0x000E3E58  91080000  lbu   $t0, 0($t0)
//       0x000E3E5C  24090001  addiu $t1, $zero, 1
//       0x000E3E60  1509000C  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E3E94
//       0x000E3E64  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3E68  4408A000  mfc1  $t0, $f20
//       0x000E3E6C  3C093F80  lui   $t1, 0x3F80
//       0x000E3E70  35290000  ori   $t1, $t1, 0
//       0x000E3E74  15090007  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E3E94
//       0x000E3E78  00000000  nop
//       0x000E3E7C  3C083F40  lui   $t0, 0x3F40
//       0x000E3E80  35080000  ori   $t0, $t0, 0
//       0x000E3E84  44886800  mtc1  $t0, $f13
//       0x000E3E88  460D6300  add.s $f12, $f12, $f13
//       0x000E3E8C  46006324  cvt.w.s $f12, $f12
//       0x000E3E90  46806320  cvt.s.w $f12, $f12
//       0x000E3E94  C7AD0020  lwc1  $f13, 32($sp)
//       0x000E3E98  7BA80000  lq    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000E3E9C  7BA90010  lq    $t1, 16($sp)
//       0x000E3EA0  27BD0030  addiu $sp, $sp, 48
//       0x000E3EA4  27BDFFD0  addiu $sp, $sp, -48
//       0x000E3EA8  3C013A80  lui   $at, 0x3A80
//       0x000E3EAC  080412F4  j     0x00104BD0
//       0x000E3EB0  00000000  nop
//
patch=1,EE,000E3E00,word,27BDFFD0
patch=1,EE,000E3E04,word,7FA80000
patch=1,EE,000E3E08,word,7FA90010
patch=1,EE,000E3E0C,word,E7AD0020
