//
//     and only now the hook, a `j` WITHOUT its delay slot: what it
//     displaces is the `lw $v1, 4($s3)` the routine replays at the end,
//     and the slot `addiu $s4, $s4, 4` runs LIVE before the jump.
//     NOPing it would eat the advance of the key pointer.
patch=1,EE,00104EA0,word,08039400

// 37. cutjump -- camera cuts by TRANSLATION.
//
//     The symptom: on a camera jump an INTERMEDIATE shot appears that
//     stock does not have. The game's cut detector (0x00355CAC..CD0)
//     only looks at ORIENTATION -- abs(dot) < 0.98 --, and here the
//     camera jumps to another place almost without turning: the game
//     does not see the cut, the 60 Hz half step interpolates between
//     the two shots, and `cutshift` and `cutpose` hold nothing, because
//     there was no cut.
//
//     This section hooks the branch `bne $a2, $zero, 0x00355CEC` that
//     follows the detector. When the detector said no and the camera's
//     position keys have this shape -- contiguous and one tick apart,
//     with the rotation at those same times, the previous key still at
//     the same XYZ for at least two ticks, and a jump of more than one
//     unit --, it leaves $a2 = 1 and $f5 = 0, the same the game leaves
//     when it recognises a cut, and exits through `cutshift`'s hook. It
//     holds nothing by itself: it tells the game. It is a heuristic on
//     the shape of the keys, not a cut flag of the format.
//
//     Guards: the caller asked for detection ($t0 on entry), dt == 1/60
//     with live divider 1, SceneUpdate's CAMERA chain (0x00356130 at
//     original stack +0x50, 0x0039CF64 at +0x60) and the track of the
//     active camera. It DEPENDS on `cutshift` and `cutpose`. At 30 fps
//     it is inert.
//
//     It preserves the 128-bit $t0..$t5, $f13..$f15 and FCR31. No
//     mutable state. The routine, in its cave:
//
//       0x000E5200  27BDFF80  addiu $sp, $sp, -128
//       0x000E5204  7FA80000  sq    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000E5208  7FA90010  sq    $t1, 16($sp)
//       0x000E520C  7FAA0020  sq    $t2, 32($sp)
//       0x000E5210  7FAB0030  sq    $t3, 48($sp)
//       0x000E5214  7FAC0040  sq    $t4, 64($sp)
//       0x000E5218  7FAD0050  sq    $t5, 80($sp)
//       0x000E521C  E7AD0060  swc1  $f13, 96($sp)
//       0x000E5220  E7AE0064  swc1  $f14, 100($sp)
//       0x000E5224  E7AF0068  swc1  $f15, 104($sp)
//       0x000E5228  4448F800  cfc1  $t0, $f31
//       0x000E522C  AFA8006C  sw    $t0, 108($sp)
//       0x000E5230  14C00063  bne   $a2, $zero, 0x000E53C0
//       0x000E5234  00000000  nop
//       0x000E5238  8FA80000  lw    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000E523C  11000060  beq   $t0, $zero, 0x000E53C0
//       0x000E5240  00000000  nop
//       0x000E5244  3C080051  lui   $t0, 0x0051
//       0x000E5248  350802CC  ori   $t0, $t0, 716
//       0x000E524C  8D080000  lw    $t0, 0($t0)
//       0x000E5250  3C093C88  lui   $t1, 0x3C88
//       0x000E5254  35298889  ori   $t1, $t1, -30583
//       0x000E5258  15090059  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E53C0
//       0x000E525C  00000000  nop
//       0x000E5260  3C080059  lui   $t0, 0x0059
//       0x000E5264  35086D70  ori   $t0, $t0, 28016
//       0x000E5268  91080000  lbu   $t0, 0($t0)
//       0x000E526C  3C090000  lui   $t1, 0x0000
//       0x000E5270  35290001  ori   $t1, $t1, 1
//       0x000E5274  15090052  bne   $t0, $t1, 0x000E53C0
