//
//     and only now the hook: the delay slot NOPed first -- the routine
//     replays the threshold's `lui`/`ori` on both its exits -- and then
//     the `j`. Without a cut it returns to 0x00355CBC (the detector goes
//     on); with a cut, to 0x00355CEC, section 28's hook.
patch=1,EE,00355CB8,word,00000000
patch=1,EE,00355CB4,word,0803A800

// 52. relocpose -- the POSE anticipates an absolute relocation. The
//     same cutscene: Vance showed up for a frame behind the group and
//     Swan for a frame in the foreground.
//
//     The resource's pose translation carries a large jump a few ticks
//     before a pair of 0x15/0x16 events (section 35's absolute
//     relocation). Section 43 (eventsnap) holds it when the pair is on
//     the NEXT tick; here it is between 1 and 4 ahead.
//
//     This section, where section 44 returns (0x00336BC8), for
//     SceneAnim's POSE channel: on the half step, if the horizontal gap
//     between the ends section 44 left in $v0/$v1 exceeds 1 u and 32
//     times the bound of the incoming motion (pose step and encoded
//     velocity), it leaves $f12 = 0, $f21 = cursor and $a1 = $f12: the
//     pose and the bones at the old end. It DEPENDS on `rootturn`,
//     `rootphase`, `scenevel`, `sceneyaw`, `scenerebase` and
//     `poseframe`. It preserves $at and the 128-bit $t0..$t5, $f0..$f5
//     and the FCR31. No mutable state. The routine, in its cave:
//
//       0x000EA400  27BDFF40  addiu $sp, $sp, -192
//       0x000EA404  7FA10000  sq    $at, 0($sp)
//       0x000EA408  7FA80010  sq    $t0, 16($sp)
//       0x000EA40C  7FA90020  sq    $t1, 32($sp)
//       0x000EA410  7FAA0030  sq    $t2, 48($sp)
//       0x000EA414  7FAB0040  sq    $t3, 64($sp)
//       0x000EA418  7FAC0050  sq    $t4, 80($sp)
