//
//     and only now the hook, a `j` WITHOUT its delay slot: the
//     `lw $v0, 0x54($a1)` runs live before the jump. The routine
//     replays the `lw $a3, 4($a0)` first and returns to 0x003A3480,
//     which is section 66's hook (sprayrate).
patch=1,EE,003A3478,word,0803BE00

// 57. menugate -- the EXIT DIALOG of Rumble > Edit Gang did not
//     respond: "Do you want to exit?" ignored the D-pad, the stick, X
//     and Triangle.
//
//     The dialog's update (0x001D4F20, vtable class 0x0053B768) only
//     reads the pad if MORE THAN 20 MS have gone by since [this+0x84],
//     against the real-time clock (ms from the EE counter). That mark
//     is written by its "activate" (0x001D4D28), and both parents that
//     have this dialog activate it on EVERY frame after the update: the
//     guard measures the interval between frames, 33 ms in stock
//     (always passes) and 16-17 at 60 fps (never passes).
//
//     The guard at 10 ms: at 60 fps it passes every frame and still
//     blocks input on the SAME frame as the activation, which is all it
//     blocked in stock. One word, the same addiu with another
//     immediate. No cave, no hook, no state.
//       0x001D4FB0  24630014 -> 2463000A  addiu $v1, $v1, 10
patch=1,EE,001D4FB0,word,2463000A

// 58. dpadrepeat -- the HELD D-PAD in menus repeated too early
//     (Rumble > Swap Player): holding a direction, the list started
//     scrolling at 233 ms instead of stock's 467.
//
//     The pad tick (0x00144FB0, the one that turns the ring) keeps one
//     counter per direction at [pad+0x30..0x33]: it rises one per tick
//     up to 15 and goes back to 12, and the accessors with repeat
//     (0x00144AD0, the menus; 0x00144C38, the action table) treat it as
//     repeated at 15. In ticks: 14 until the first repeat and 4 between
//     repeats; at 60 Hz, half the time.
//
//     The counter counts double: it fires at 29 and goes back to 22,
//     and the readers compare with 29. 28 ticks = 467 ms, 8 = 133 ms,
//     like stock. The 16 constants are each the same instruction with
//     another immediate; they go all together or not at all. No cave,
//     no hook, no state.
//       0x00145248  2C62000F -> 2C62001D  sltiu $v0, $v1, 29
//       0x0014525C  2402000C -> 24020016  addiu $v0, $zero, 22
//       0x0014527C  2C62000F -> 2C62001D  sltiu $v0, $v1, 29
//       0x00145290  2402000C -> 24020016  addiu $v0, $zero, 22
//       0x001452B0  2C62000F -> 2C62001D  sltiu $v0, $v1, 29
//       0x001452C4  2402000C -> 24020016  addiu $v0, $zero, 22
//       0x001452E4  2C62000F -> 2C62001D  sltiu $v0, $v1, 29
//       0x001452F8  2402000C -> 24020016  addiu $v0, $zero, 22
//       0x00144B14  3842000F -> 3842001D  xori  $v0, $v0, 29
//       0x00144B2C  3842000F -> 3842001D  xori  $v0, $v0, 29
//       0x00144B44  3842000F -> 3842001D  xori  $v0, $v0, 29
//       0x00144B5C  3842000F -> 3842001D  xori  $v0, $v0, 29
//       0x00144C64  2402000F -> 2402001D  addiu $v0, $zero, 29
//       0x00144C84  2402000F -> 2402001D  addiu $v0, $zero, 29
//       0x00144C9C  2402000F -> 2402001D  addiu $v0, $zero, 29
//       0x00144CB4  2403000F -> 2403001D  addiu $v1, $zero, 29
patch=1,EE,00145248,word,2C62001D
patch=1,EE,0014525C,word,24020016
patch=1,EE,0014527C,word,2C62001D
patch=1,EE,00145290,word,24020016
patch=1,EE,001452B0,word,2C62001D
patch=1,EE,001452C4,word,24020016
