// 61. creditrate -- the end CREDITS scrolled at double speed (Come Out
//     to Play, the final cutscene and the credits).
//
//     The credits update (0x001A9E90, the object HUD+0xEA30) moves each
//     line 0.0025 of the screen up PER UPDATE, without dt: 30 times per
//     second in stock, 60 patched. Building new lines, freeing the ones
//     that leave and the ending all go by position.
//
//     The function that moves one line (0x001A9B70, a single caller)
//     takes half the step: its mov.s becomes a multiply by the 0.5 the
//     caller already has in $f20. One word, no cave, no hook, no state.
//       0x001A9B8C  46006506 -> 46146502  mul.s $f20, $f12, $f20
patch=1,EE,001A9B8C,word,46146502

// 62. shakerate -- the camera SHAKE of explosions, at double speed
//     (Destroyed, Virgil's third phase, the fireballs): the shake was
//     shorter and stronger.
//
//     The common shake routine (0x00121298) raises and lowers the
//     envelopes, counts down the timers and draws the random offset PER
//     UPDATE: at 60 fps, twice as often.
//
//     Three hooks, at 60 fps (divider 1 and camera dt 1/60) with ANY
//     global dt, slow motion included: on the odd frame it does not
//     update the channels or draw (it reuses the previous offset); the
//     timer drops 2 * camera dt * min(2 * factor, 1), the native factor
//     recomputed with stock's dt: stock's decrement. Every camera shake,
//     not only the ones in this level. In the slow motion of Cowboy's
//     finisher the shake lasts 967 ms, like stock. It preserves the
//     128-bit $t0-$t1; no state. The addresses 0x000F5000/5200/5400 are
//     reserved and left unused.
//
//       0x000F5100  27BDFFE0  addiu $sp, $sp, -32
//       0x000F5104  7FA80000  sq    $t0, 0($sp)
//       0x000F5108  7FA90010  sq    $t1, 16($sp)
//       0x000F510C  3C080059  lui   $t0, 0x0059
//       0x000F5110  35086D70  ori   $t0, $t0, 28016
