// 64. knifeslow -- the SLOW MOTION of the knife at Luther came late
//     (Come Out to Play, Swan throws the knife with Square+X).
//
//     The boss's tactic sets the global timestep to 1/60 for one second
//     and to 1/120 for four: in stock, at 30 updates per second, half
//     speed and then a quarter. At 60, 1/60 IS normal speed: the first
//     second did not slow down and then it slowed to half. Both lui go
//     to half, like section 3's constants: 1/120 and 1/240. No cave, no
//     hook, no state.
//       0x0030C8CC  3C013C88 -> 3C013C08  lui   $at, 0x3C08
//       0x0030C924  3C013C08 -> 3C013B88  lui   $at, 0x3B88
patch=1,EE,0030C8CC,word,3C013C08
patch=1,EE,0030C924,word,3C013B88

// 65. knifechord -- throwing the KNIFE with Square + X missed stock's
//     window (Swan with a knife in front of the dealer): with X and
//     Square almost together, sometimes a common punch came out instead
//     of the throw.
//
//     Section 22 (chord30) decides chords on the 30 Hz grid, and that
//     delayed the throw by a frame: the common Square got ahead, and
//     the held X could override it. Three hooks on the action
//     classifier, ONLY at normal 60 fps with chord30 and with a knife in
//     the player's hand: the Square edge goes on the same grid, and the
//     held X does not override the throw before three stock samples. It
//     depends on section 22. No state.
//
//     The same chord drives the GRAPPLE attack (Square + X while
//     grabbing an enemy), and it was lost the same way. So the guard
//     also applies with nothing in hand when the player grabs, from the
//     front or from behind, another human who is in turn grabbed by
//     him; the wrappers call it there. An older guard at 0x000F4600 is
//     left unused. The four routines, in their caves:
//
